{"uid":"484a7a3f4b5a08b2","name":"test_a_worker_writable_workspace_file_cannot_supply_the_answer","fullName":"tests.test_finding_curability#test_a_worker_writable_workspace_file_cannot_supply_the_answer","historyId":"de7af420d2381153136140eab5189723","time":{"start":1791980637040,"stop":1791980637044,"duration":4},"description":"Construct the two directories a real run actually has -- an\n    engine-owned run dir (`RunDir.root`, where review's own\n    `review-findings.json` lives) and a separate, WORKER-writable\n    workspace (`LoopSupervisor.workspace`, the directory mounted into the\n    worker's own container). Write a file into the worker-writable\n    workspace that -- if anything in the answer path read it -- would flip\n    an all-incurable rejection to \"curable\" (and vice versa for a second\n    case). The answer must be identical whether or not that file exists,\n    because `all_blocking_findings_incurable` never opens any file at all;\n    it only ever sees the `findings` argument its caller passes it.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Construct the two directories a real run actually has -- an<br />\nengine-owned run dir (<code>RunDir.root</code>, where review's own<br />\n<code>review-findings.json</code> lives) and a separate, WORKER-writable<br />\nworkspace (<code>LoopSupervisor.workspace</code>, the directory mounted into the<br />\nworker's own container). Write a file into the worker-writable<br />\nworkspace that -- if anything in the answer path read it -- would flip<br />\nan all-incurable rejection to &quot;curable&quot; (and vice versa for a second<br />\ncase). The answer must be identical whether or not that file exists,<br />\nbecause <code>all_blocking_findings_incurable</code> never opens any file at all;<br />\nit only ever sees the <code>findings</code> argument its caller passes it.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name"